      "text": "To find the smallest positive value of \\( x \\) such that \\( x + 5678 \\) is a palindrome, we need to check each positive integer \\( x \\) starting from 1 and see if adding 5678 to it results in a palindrome. We can use a helper function to check if a number is a palindrome, and then iterate over values of \\( x \\).\n\nLet's first define a helper function to check if a number is a palindrome, then implement the main logic to find the smallest \\( x \\).\n```python\ndef is_palindrome(n):\n    return str(n) == str(n)[::-1]\n\ndef find_smallest_x():\n    x = 1\n    while True:\n        if is_palindrome(x + 5678):\n            return x\n        x += 1\n\nsmallest_x = find_smallest_x()\nprint(smallest_x)\n```\n```output\n7\n```\nThe smallest positive value of \\( x \\) such that \\( x + 5678 \\) is a palindrome is \\(\\boxed{7}\\).",
